{"finish_reason":"stop","model":"root","text":"### Where it’s sized\n\nWhen the context is created. `llama_init_from_model()` reads `n_ctx` from the context parameters and allocates the cache for that many tokens up front, for every layer. Nothing grows later.\n\n### What it costs on this Mac\n\n| Window | Cache, 8-bit | With weights |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| 8K | 0.2 GB | 12.3 GB |\n| 32K | 0.6 GB | 12.7 GB |\n| 128K | 2.4 GB | 14.5 GB |\n\nApogee picks 32K on this machine and keeps the cache 8-bit. `apogee models info gpt-oss-20b` prints the same arithmetic.","turn":1,"type":"result"}
